                "text": "To solve  \n\\[\n\\sin(x)+x^2=42,\n\\]\nrewrite it as finding zeros of\n\\[\nf(x)=\\sin(x)+x^2-42.\n\\]\n\nBecause \\(x^2\\approx 42\\) suggests \\(x\\approx \\pm\\sqrt{42}\\approx \\pm 6.48\\), we look for roots near those values. Using a numerical root-finder gives two real solutions:\n\n\\[\nx \\approx 6.4666500409\n\\]\nand\n\\[\nx \\approx -6.4970982170.\n\\]\n\nSo the equation has **two real solutions**: \\(\\boxed{x \\approx 6.46665 \\text{ and } x \\approx -6.49710}\\).",
